  "notes": "Owner-supplied brand artwork, not a third-party asset: the black-and-white source is recorded by digest in apps/workbench/brand/PROVENANCE.json (source sha256 71be068292b4882c..., 1344x1384). The owner's instruction on 2026-10-08 was to cut the mark out of its ground and use it in the interface, which is the basis for commercialUse (it ships in the product UI) and modelInputAllowed (the file was handed to the session that extracted it). redistributable stays false: no statement was made about carrying the mark outside this project, and the brand's own licensing is the owner's to declare. expiresAt is the annual asset re-verification interval, not an owner deadline. The tracked file is the extracted 144x144 cut-out; the same bytes are inlined into apps/workbench/style.css as --brand-mark and kept in sync by design-lab/scripts/render_brand_asset.py --check."
